<h2>Notice and Wonder</h2>
<p><strong>Original 2021 learning goal:</strong> Apply understanding of equal groups to create a Notice and Wonder activity.</p>
<p>Warm-up Notice and Wonder: Equal Groups (10 minutes). The original locally referenced image has attribution to Virginie Duboscq via Pixabay; original pixels were not inspected. Invite multiple grounded mathematical observations and questions, without assuming a specific visible object count.</p>
<h3>Notice and Wonder: Equal Groups</h3><p>Examine the original instructor-provided image and offer observations and questions; do not infer unverified object counts. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Design Your Notice and Wonder</h3><p>Choose a suitable equal-groups photo and prepare possible observations and questions. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
<h3>Facilitate Your Notice and Wonder</h3><p>Display your chosen photo, provide discussion time, then record classmates&#x27; contributions. Teacher evaluates actual cards, drawings, images, and oral work where required.</p>
